 208:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h **** /**
 209:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  * This is a variant of mavlink_frame_char() but with caller supplied
 210:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  * parsing buffers. It is useful when you want to create a MAVLink
 211:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  * parser in a library that doesn't use any global variables
 212:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  *
 213:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  * @param rxmsg    parsing message buffer
 214:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  * @param status   parsing status buffer 
 215:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  * @param c        The char to parse
 216:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  *
 217:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  * @param r_message NULL if no message could be decoded, otherwise the message data
 218:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  * @param r_mavlink_status if a message was decoded, this is filled with the channel's stats
